ERRATUM (added 2026-08-14, after push).

This commit's message describes only the sdist packaging fix and the repo/doc
hygiene. It also contains, unannounced, the whole of the source-hygiene work
(bead lob-7ig plus the source items of lob-kbx), because the orchestrator ran
`git add -A` while a second agent was still writing to src/. Nothing was lost
and ./verify was green at the time, but the message does not describe the diff.

What is actually in here beyond the stated scope:

- src/PyLOB/engine.py: quantize/clipPrice alias flipped so the modern name is
  the definition; _check_working_price extracted from two verbatim copies;
  BookSide.best_level and total_volume removed; takers/makers renamed to
  taker_book/maker_book; naming glosses on fulfilled and the three counters.
- BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: configure_instrument(symbol, currency) now raises
  InvalidOrder when symbol == currency. Both legs would otherwise post to one
  (tid, symbol) balance key and net silently. This enforces a constraint
  openspec/config.yaml already states rather than inventing one, and refuses at
  the gate before any state changes, so it emits no event.
- src/PyLOB/events.py: Filled.taker_idNum/maker_idNum removed (no callers);
  commission_max_percnt 'sic' note.
- src/PyLOB/bench/provenance.py: effective_ghz and CoreClock.ipc removed;
  request_performance_core collapsed; _repo_root made public as repo_root().
- src/PyLOB/__init__.py: __version__ added.
- tests/test_emission_coverage.py: two label strings following the alias flip.

Deliberately NOT changed, and recorded because the reasoning matters: read
queries still create an instrument on first mention. openspec/config.yaml's
constraint block states that behaviour as what the frozen specs are written
against, so changing it is an OpenSpec delta rather than a code fix. It is
documented loudly in book() instead.
